        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "As we start 1a, we struggle to understand its technical terms at the same time we are hacking through a subject twenty-two words long. In 1b, we go through just three words to get past the subject and verb and twelve more before we hit a term—sociometric—that might slow us down. By that point we have enough momentum to carry us through the complexity to the sentence's end. That's because 1b begins simply and saves its more complex grammatical constructions and concepts for later.",
